            (
            %a{:href => "#ConnerFloyd66"}> Conner-Floyd 66, Theorem 16.2
            )
          %p
            The first step in the proof of
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ToddClassesOnShortExactSequenceOfUFrBordismRings"} (19)
            is the observation (
            %a{:href => "#ConnerFloyd66"}> Conner-Floyd 66, p. 100-101
            ) that the representing map
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:InTermsOfHomotopyGroupsOfQuotientedThomSpace"} (17)
            for a
            = succeed "-manifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi fr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U,fr)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^{2k}
            cobounding a
            = succeed "-manifold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fr
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fr
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is given by the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+diagram"} homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagram"} pasting diagram
            (see also at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant"} Hopf invariant
                –
                %a{:href => "Hopf+invariant#InGeneralizedCohomology"} In generalized cohomology
          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 20px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:alt => "homotopy pasting diagram exhibiting cobounding UFr-manifolds", :src => "/nlab/files/CoboundingUFrManifoldDiagrammatically.jpg", :width => "470px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Equivariant+Cohomotopy+and+Oriented+Cohomology+Theory"} SS21
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#KOVersion
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi KO
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = KO
          %h3#the_adams_invariant_in__2
            The Adams
            = succeed "-invariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{\mathbb{R}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z}
          %p
          #eRInvariantInTermsOfAdamsOperations.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#eInvariantInComplexTopologicalKtheoryAsRationalNumberModuloIntegers"}
              (via
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+operations"} Adams operations
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
              in place of complex topological K-theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{\mathbb{R}}
              (
              %a{:href => "#Adams66"}> Adams 66, p. 39
              ).
            %p
          %p
            But beware that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{\mathbb{R}}
            may fail to be equal to the coefficient of the top degree Chern character on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin+character"} Pontrjagin character
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#eRInvariantIsNotInGeneralTopDegreeChernCharacter"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{\mathbb{R}}
            a finer invariant: It is either equal to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{\mathbb{C}}
            or to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tfrac{1}{2}e_{\mathbb{C}}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Adams66"} Adams 66 (7.3)
          %h3#as_a_cobordism_invariant_of_manifolds_with_framed_boundary
            As a cobordism invariant of
            = succeed "-manifolds" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU
          %p
            An analogous but finer version of the
            = succeed "-theoretic" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theory"} cobordism
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AsACobordismInvariantOfManifoldsWithBoundary"} above
            = succeed "-structure" do
