            %br/
          %h2#ConstructionViaUnitCofiberTheories Diagrammatic construction
          %blockquote
            %p under construction – not complete yet
          %p
            While the Adams e-invariant of a map exists when the its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/d-invariant"} d-invariant
            vanishes, the classical constructions above implicitly proceed via a finer invariant of maps
            %em equipped with a trivialization
            of their d-invariant. In order to bring this out more explicitly, the following is meant to be another, more abstractly homotopy theoretic, way to approach the construction of the e-invariant (following
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/M-Theory+as+Mf-Theory"} SS21
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            and Conner-Floyd’s construction via the Todd character on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MUFr"} MUFr
