          %h3#UnitCofiberCohomologyTheory Unit cofiber cohomology theory
          %p
          #UnitCofiberCohomologyTheory.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p [Unit cofiber cohomology theory]
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative cohomology theory
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} represented
              by a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy-commutative+ring+spectrum"} homotopy-commutative ring spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi E
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S} \overset{ e^E }{\longrightarrow} E
              we denote the corresponding
              = succeed "-theory" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber"} homotopy cofiber
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi 𝕊
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E/\mathbb{S}
            %p
              (In notation common around the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
              this would be “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \overline {E}
              ” – as in
              %a{:href => "Adams+spectral+sequence#Adams74"} Adams 74, theorem 15.1 page 319
              – or just “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{ E }
              ” – as in
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Adams+spectral+sequence#Hopkins99"} Hopkins 99, Cor. 5.3
            %p
              Via the induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+cofiber+sequence"} homotopy cofiber sequence
