              yields the induced cohomology operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi/\mathbb{S}
              on cofiber theories (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnitCofiberCohomologyTheory"}
          %p
          #ChernCharacterOnCofiberOfKTheory.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              [Chern character on cofiber of K-theory] The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
              operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} KU
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ϕ
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ev
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{KU} \overset{\phi}{\longrightarrow} H^{\mathrm{ev}}\mathbb{Q}
              is multiplicative, hence passes to an operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
