            %p
              For given
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                        %mi E
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^E_{n-1}\!(c)
              %em single
              cell and “rectangle” for the pasting composite of any adjacent
              %em pair
              of them):
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The two squares on the left are the stabilization of the homotopy pushout squares defining the cofiber space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_c
                  and the suspension of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mi d
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n + d - 1}
              %li
                %p
                  The bottom left rectangle (with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Σ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^n(e^E)
                  at its top) is the homotopy pushout defining
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi 𝕊
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^n(E\!/\mathbb{S})
              %li
                %p
                  The classifying map for the given
                  = succeed "-flux," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathcolor => "magenta"}
                          %msup
                            %mi M
                            %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\color{magenta}M^d}
                  forming the bottom middle square is uniquely implied by the homotopy pushout property of the bottom left square. Moreover, the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
                  implies that this bottom middle square is itself homotopy cartesian.
              %li
                %p
                  The bottom right square is the homotopy pushout defining
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial
              %li
                %p
                  By the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
                  it follows that also the bottom right rectangle is homotopy cocartesian, hence that, after the two squares on the left, it exhibits the third step in the long homotopy cofiber sequence of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mn ∞
                          %mi c
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty c
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mrow
                              %mn ∞
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mi c
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^{\infty + 1} c
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∂
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi M
                            %mi d
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \big[ M^d \big] = [c]
            %p
              In conclusion, these construction steps yield a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                      %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi M
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^E_{n-1}\!(c) \mapsto M^d
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn ∞
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma^\infty c]
            %p
          %p
          #LiftedEInvariantDiagrammatically.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              The
              %em refined e-invariant
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi e
                        %mo ^
                      %mi KU
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat e_{KU}
              is the composite of
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the equivalence from Prop.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EFluxesAreCocycleInCofiberTheory"}
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo =
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E =
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
              %li
                %p
                  the cofiber Chern character from Example
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ChernCharacterOnCofiberOfKTheory"}
              %li
                %p
                  the canonical splitting from Remark
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CanonicalSplittingOfCofiberOfPeriodicRationalCohomology"}
