          %p
            using that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/the+rational+Todd+class+is+the+Chern+character+of+the+Thom+class"} the rational Todd class is the Chern character of the Thom class
            and that this identification is represented by a corresponding factorization of maps of multiplicative cohomology theories, as shown (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "rational+Todd+class+is+Chern+character+of+Thom+class#Smith73"} Smith 73, Section 1
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#ThirdStableStem Third stable homotopy group of spheres
          #AdamseRInvariantDetectsThirdStableHomotopyGroupOfSpheres.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#Adams66"}> Adams 66, Example 7.17 and p. 46
                )
            %p
              In degree 3, the
              = succeed "-theoretic" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/e-invariant"} e-invariant
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{\mathbb{R}}
              takes the value
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 24
                      %mo ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left[\tfrac{1}{24}\right] \in \mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z}
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi ℍ
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7 \overset{h_{\mathbb{H}}}{\longrightarrow} S^4
              and hence reflects the full
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/third+stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres"} third stable homotopy group of spheres
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi π
                              %mn 3
                              %mi s
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mo ≃
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi e
                                  %mi ℝ
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mn 24
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⊂
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℚ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi ℤ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi h
                              %mi ℍ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo [
                              %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                %mfrac
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mn 24
                              %mo ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\pi^s_3
                    \&amp;
                    \\underoverset{
                    \\simeq
                    }{
                    e_{\mathbb{R}}
                    }{
                    \\;\;\longrightarrow\;\;
                    }
                    \&amp;
                    \\mathbb{Z}/24
                    \&amp;
                    \\subset
                    \&amp;
                    \\mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z}
                    \\\
                    [h_{\mathbb{H}}]
                    \&amp;&amp;\mapsto&amp;&amp;
                    \\left[\tfrac{1}{24}\right]
                    }
            %p
              while
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_{\mathbb{C}}
              sees only “half” of it (by
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Adams66"} Adams 66, Prop. 7.14
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eta-invariant"} eta-invariant
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/d-invariant"}> d-invariant
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/f-invariant"} f-invariant
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant"}> Hopf invariant
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant+one+problem"} Hopf invariant one problem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-homomorphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} stable homotopy groups of spheres
          %h2#references References
          %p The definition is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Adams66
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Adams"}> John Adams
                , Sections 3,7 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    On the groups
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(X)
                    IV
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.unice.fr/~cazanave/Gdt/ImJ/J-IV.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383(66)90004-8"} doi:10.1016/0040-9383(66)90004-8
              %p
                %em> Correction
                , Topology 7 (3): 331 (1968)
          %p
            Discussion in more general
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+generalized+cohomology+theories"} Whitehead generalized cohomology theories
          %ul
            %li#Krueger73
              %p
                Warren M. Krueger,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized Steenrod-Hopf Invariants for Stable Homotopy Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2039603"} jstor:2039603
            %li
              %p
                Warren M. Krueger,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Relation with the Hopf invariant revisited
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.ijm/1256047713"} euclid:ijm/1256047713
          %p
            and in relation to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
          %ul
            %li#Switzer75
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Switzer"}> Robert Switzer
              , Section 19.19 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic Topology - Homotopy and Homology
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-642-61923-6"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-61923-6
          %p
            and to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/f-invariant"} f-invariant
          %ul
            %li#BL09
              Mark Behrens, Gerd Laures,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
                  \-Family congruences and the
                  = succeed "-invariant" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0809.1125"} arXiv:0809.1125
              = succeed ")" do
